.TH SIRENE 1 "November 2026" "Sirène 0.1.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sirene \- settings for HUAWEI FreeBuds earphones on GNOME (Sirène)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sirene
[\fIOPTION\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sirène sets HUAWEI FreeBuds earphones (6i, 7i, 4i) over their own Bluetooth
channel: noise control, gestures, equalizer, sound, wear detection, dual
connect, batteries. It finds the earphones on its own when they connect, pauses
the players when an earbud is taken out, and can stay in the background with an
icon in the top bar. If Sirène is already running, a new launch shows its window.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-background
Start without a window (used at login).
.TP
.BI \-\-anc= MODE
Set the noise control of the connected earphones: \fBoff\fR, \fBcancellation\fR, \fBawareness\fR, or
\fBnext\fR for the next mode. Meant for a keyboard shortcut (GNOME Settings, Keyboard, Custom Shortcuts).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sirene/settings.json
Preferences.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/io.github.sirene.Sirene.desktop
Start at login (Preferences).
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/ToFpon/Sirene
